From 611ffddb7fbb6b539fea24026942b4b905c8472b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:19:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Render quick-settings tiles as static black ink on white
 paper

Change-Id: I547fa9dc6cc0602c70c4944171ae5c30e7042ed6

Replace the outline layer by id instead of a hard-coded index.

Compose quick settings tiles (folded from 0022-black-one-pixel-notification-outline, formerly feature qs-outline): the Compose QS Tile draws the same 1 px black outline, so both the legacy QSTileViewImpl and the Compose renderer (infinitegrid/Tile.kt) show static outlined tiles.

Brightness slider: grey inactive track on flat devices (surfaceEffect1 is white).

Brightness: on flat devices the slider background (also the drag mirror and brightness dialog over apps) and the auto-brightness button when off get a whole-pixel edge.

Compose QS tiles: whole-pixel edge in the theme ink (EinkSurfaces) instead of a hard-coded black pixel; unavailable tiles get a grey edge; the toggle target of dual-target tiles is ringed. Edit mode: edit tiles, the available-tiles list (one edge) and the overflow menu are outlined. Footer: the security/FGS pills and the inactive icon buttons are outlined. Modes dialog tiles are outlined.

Dropped the View QS tile hunks (QSTileViewImpl, QSIconViewImpl, EinkUi): with the Compose QS fragment they never run.
